WEBVTT

00:11:27.812 --> 00:11:31.231
This purse is also a reminder that the things that you imagine,

00:11:31.231 --> 00:11:34.773
sitting in your office or in the library,

00:11:34.773 --> 00:11:37.176
are not how you find them when you actually go out

00:11:37.176 --> 00:11:38.683
into the world.

00:11:38.683 --> 00:11:40.671
Thank you. (Applause)

00:11:40.671 --> 00:11:47.343
(Applause)

00:11:47.343 --> 00:11:49.412
Chris Anderson: Thank you, Leslie, that was an insight

00:11:49.412 --> 00:11:52.009
that a lot of us haven't had before.

00:11:52.009 --> 00:11:55.496
But I'm curious. If you had a minute, say,

00:11:55.496 --> 00:11:59.217
with Apple's head of manufacturing,

00:11:59.217 --> 00:12:01.577
what would you say?